# Template for /etc/dyx3/ros.env — read by dyx3-ros, dyx3-recorder, dyx3-rtk and dyx3-spray-watchdog. Created once by the installer; an upgrade never
# overwrites it.
#
# REQUIRED. The architecture pins the ROS domain but names no number: choose one that no other rover / laptop on your network uses, then
# uncomment. The launchers refuse to start while this is unset (they never guess).
#ROS_DOMAIN_ID=
#
# OPEN (architecture 4.4 "DDS scoped to eth0"): the ROS graph is local to the Jetson, so loopback-only is stricter than an eth0 whitelist and
# survives an unplugged FCU cable. Set to 1 to restrict DDS to loopback.
#DYX3_ROS_LOCALHOST_ONLY=1
